id: pm-gh1660
title: "GH-1660: the project telemetry block pm init writes is inert, so the wizard's telemetry decline and the project endpoint are ignored, and no supported way points opted-in tests at a local collector"
description: "GitHub issue #1660 (reported 2026-11-04 against 2026.11.4). docs/CONFIGURATION.md 'Test environments' says PM_TELEMETRY_SOURCE_CONTEXT or PM_TELEMETRY_SEND_TEST_EVENTS=1 permits intentional test delivery and tells authors to point such tests at a local collector, but nothing supported does that. No environment variable overrides the event endpoint (SENTRY_DSN redirects Sentry and OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_* redirects spans; PM_TELEMETRY_INGEST_KEY is auth only). pm config project/global set telemetry.endpoint refuses with invalid_argument_value. pm init writes a full telemetry block, including the production endpoint, into the project settings.json, yet editing that value has no effect: pm ops telemetry status still reports the production endpoint, because the effective telemetry settings are read from the global profile only (src/core/store/settings.ts resolves endpoint from the global settings). Only hand-editing the global profile changes status.endpoint. Impact: an extension test that followed the documented opt-in delivered its expected refusals to production Sentry (PM-CLI-3R..3X, environment=test), which blocked the 2026.11.4 auto-release Sentry gate; the release-gate side is owned by pm-usn5k2 and the extension side by unbraind/pm-vcs#176. Duplicate check: searched telemetry endpoint/override/local collector/project settings across all statuses; the closed telemetry env-var and pipeline items document the opt-out surface but no endpoint override."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: configuration,docs,ecosystem,sentry,telemetry
created_at: "2026-11-04T11:24:47.413Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T19:11:09.292Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-04T16:25:45.285Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-04T16:25:45.285Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A documented environment override (for example PM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT) points event delivery at another collector, validated like the settings endpoint and reported in pm ops telemetry status env_overrides; The project-level telemetry block is either honored for the endpoint or no longer written by pm init, and a spec shows status.endpoint matches what actually receives events; docs/CONFIGURATION.md Test environments names the supported override next to SENTRY_DSN and OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_*; The pm init wizard's telemetry answer governs delivery for that user: a decline is persisted where the telemetry runtime reads consent (the global profile), never only in the project file, with a spec that drives the wizard answer n and asserts the effective status is disabled; pm config project set telemetry-tracking refuses with a remedy naming pm config global set telemetry-tracking, because the runtime reads consent only from the global profile, instead of reporting changed=true for a value nothing reads; The documented opt-out pm config set telemetry-tracking off, with no explicit scope, takes effect for the CLI install when run inside a project (the shorthand resolves to the global profile), with a CLI spec asserting status configured_enabled=false afterwards"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Every project-level telemetry surface was inert, because the runtime reads consent and endpoint only from the global profile. The init wizard now persists its answer with persistGlobalTelemetryConsent and asks only while no consent is recorded and no environment opt-out applies, so it never overrides an earlier choice. writeSettings gains omitSections, which never removes a section the stored file already has. defaultConfigScope routes a scope-less telemetry-tracking call, from the CLI shorthand or MCP, to the global profile. Project-scope get and set refuse with invalid_argument_value (reason telemetry_consent_is_global), and project list and export omit the key, so ConfigResult.values is Partial. Health reads the global profile. PM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT accepts only absolute http(s) URLs, and any other value disables delivery. Override events and delivery state use files keyed by the override (telemetryRuntimeFileName). Each flush resolves the override once, for both file and target. Span state and alias usage stay in the shared state file, and idle override files are pruned after a day. Diagnostics redact endpoint credentials. An independent review agent ran five rounds to zero findings, including two P1 routing defects that round 1 found in an earlier per-entry-stamp design."
expected_result: "A user's telemetry choice, made through the wizard, the documented opt-out or config, takes effect for the CLI install, and opted-in tests deliver only to the collector PM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT names"
actual_result: "Wizard decline: global consent disabled. pm config set telemetry-tracking off: scope global, configured_enabled false. Events under PM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT reached a local listener, and an invalid value disabled delivery. All of this was checked end to end on the built CLI in a disposable profile, and the specs fail without each fix."
component: telemetry
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
